###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - No training, data set or hyperparameter setting (Q2-Q6, Q8, Q9 empty). The model is 'the pretrained MACE-MP-0 foundation model with the medium model size', with D3(BJ) dispersion added; no release is named, so it is not linked to a registry model (cf. nam2025).
# - The reported accuracy is on specific heat capacities against the DFT values of ref. 33 (PBE-D3(BJ) in CP2K, numerical frequencies with phonopy): MAE 0.10 J/(g K) and mean relative absolute error 12.18%, reduced to 0.02 J/(g K) and 2.86% with an empirical frequency scaling factor of 1.18. Heat capacity has no MetricProperty, so this is not encoded.
# - The Hessian accuracy study (maximum and mean absolute error of numerical against automatic-differentiation Hessians as a function of step size and precision) and the timing comparison on supercells of one MOF are about the differentiation scheme, not about the potential.
# - Cell optimisation with the Frechet cell filter and BFGS to 0.005 eV/A and harmonic vibrational analysis from the Hessian are the grounds for GeometryOptimization and PhononCalculation.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
